Chapter: TextOrderRefused
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ordering a Text is refused at CHECK. Before the refusal these operators
 reached a machine cmp on two POINTERS, so the answer followed allocation
 order: two separately built copies of "a" compared unequal and one of them
 was less than the other.

 The character case is a separate file on purpose. A refusal with more than
 one sufficient cause cannot be attributed to either of them, so a single
 test naming CDX2089 would pass with half the change reverted.

Section: Refused

  ta : Text = "a"

  tb : Text = "b"

  bad-lt : Boolean
  bad-lt = ta < tb

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show bad-lt)
  end

